course: dictionary
lesson: 9863
title: Synonyms: words that mean nearly the same
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A synonym is a word that means the same as another word, or almost the same. «Big» and «large» are synonyms, and so are «quick» and «fast». Finding synonyms helps you avoid repeating the same word.
explain: Synonyms are rarely exactly the same. «The dog was big.» tells us the size, but «The dog was enormous.» is much stronger. To check a synonym, swap it into the sentence and read it again: does it still make sense, and does it say what you mean?
explain: In English, a thesaurus helps you find synonyms, so «said» can become whispered, shouted or replied. In maths, many words are synonyms for the same operation: plus, add, sum and total all mean adding.
fact: A synonym is a word with nearly the same meaning as another word.
fact: «Big» and «large» are synonyms; «quick» and «fast» are synonyms.
fact: A thesaurus gives words with similar meanings, but not every synonym fits every sentence.
fact: In maths, «plus», «add», «sum», «total» and «altogether» all mean adding.
fact: «Minus», «take away» and «difference» all mean subtracting.
exercise: Which word is a synonym for «big»? | quick | small | soft | *large
exercise: Which word is a synonym for «quick»? | *fast | heavy | cold | slow
exercise: Which word means adding in maths? | minus | *total | difference | take away
test: Why might a writer swap «said» for «whispered»? | It means exactly the same, so there is no reason | *It shows how the words were spoken, quietly | It is a longer word, so it is better | It means the person was shouting
test: Which two words are both synonyms for subtracting in maths? | plus and total | *minus and difference | big and large | sum and add
exam: Which statement is true? | Synonyms are opposites of each other | Synonyms always mean exactly the same | *Synonyms have nearly the same meaning, but not always the same strength or feeling | Synonyms are only found in maths
